1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:03,940
From Records, open Manage
and select Report exports.

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:09,439
This area defines a repeatable output
file: its columns, format and scope.

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:13,279
The page also explains that exports
can be attached to a Workflow

4
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:15,149
step or placed on a schedule.

5
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:20,059
This lesson configures and checks the
file locally; it does not send an email

6
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:22,510
or upload anything to an outside agency.

7
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:26,590
Select New export to prepare a
separate training-record handoff.

8
00:00:26,999 --> 00:00:30,049
Enter a meaningful Export
name and a stable Key.

9
00:00:30,479 --> 00:00:35,079
The example is Training record handoff,
with an academy training handoff key.

10
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:39,189
The help requires lower-case
letters, digits and hyphens, and

11
00:00:39,189 --> 00:00:43,429
explains that a Workflow step or
agency import may rely on this key.

12
00:00:43,849 --> 00:00:47,660
Keep that relationship in mind before
changing names in a live integration.

13
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:51,710
Add a description of exactly what
this file is intended to contain.

14
00:00:52,099 --> 00:00:55,890
Here the description explicitly
limits the exercise to fictional

15
00:00:55,890 --> 00:00:58,650
training-record identity, state and dates.

16
00:00:58,829 --> 00:01:03,879
Use C S V as the Format, and choose
the window scope for finalized records.

17
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:06,600
Check Training under Record definitions.

18
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:10,310
The help says that leaving every
definition unchecked would export

19
00:01:10,390 --> 00:01:13,860
all definitions, so select the
intended scope deliberately.

20
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,720
For File name, enter the template token
followed by the date token, as shown.

21
00:01:19,189 --> 00:01:23,720
Keep the comma Delimiter, include a
header row, and leave Enabled checked.

22
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,759
These settings define the
file layout that the receiving

23
00:01:26,759 --> 00:01:28,480
process will need to recognize.

24
00:01:28,699 --> 00:01:33,060
Review Columns rather than accepting
an unnecessarily broad output.

25
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:38,860
Select Record number, Record type,
State, Duration in minutes, Finalized

26
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:41,440
in U T C, and Course from records.

27
00:01:41,839 --> 00:01:44,039
The screenshot shows those six checks.

28
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:49,400
Other identity, participant and incident
fields remain unselected in this example.

29
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:53,660
Choose the smallest useful set
for your actual handoff and agree

30
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:55,119
its meaning with the recipient.

31
00:01:55,539 --> 00:02:00,219
A consistent set of fields makes repeated
exports easier to compare and import.

32
00:02:00,359 --> 00:02:03,790
Scroll through the narrative and
restricted sections before saving.

33
00:02:04,169 --> 00:02:07,669
This exercise leaves all their
column checkboxes unselected.

34
00:02:08,010 --> 00:02:11,899
It also leaves Include narrative
and personal detail, Include

35
00:02:11,899 --> 00:02:15,170
restricted sections, and the
acknowledgement about sending that

36
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:17,449
content outside Resgrid unchecked.

37
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:20,549
These are separate controls
beneath the column catalog.

38
00:02:20,949 --> 00:02:24,010
Review them together with the
selected columns and the intended

39
00:02:24,010 --> 00:02:27,160
Workflow destination when
planning an actual integration.

40
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:31,320
Our local file contains none of
those narrative or restricted fields.

41
00:02:31,510 --> 00:02:35,869
For the first test, use No schedule
and set Window to thirty days.

42
00:02:36,289 --> 00:02:40,950
The help explains that zero instead uses
the schedule period ending at the run.

43
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,290
Select Save after reviewing
the prepared settings.

44
00:02:44,690 --> 00:02:48,239
The saved template can be reopened
with the same format, Training

45
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:50,190
selection and thirty-day window.

46
00:02:50,599 --> 00:02:54,419
The Report exports index confirms
The export was saved and lists

47
00:02:54,419 --> 00:02:56,269
the window scope with No schedule.

48
00:02:56,669 --> 00:03:00,429
Saving the template establishes
the configuration; it does not

49
00:03:00,429 --> 00:03:03,719
prove that the resulting file
contains the expected records.

50
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:06,990
Open Runs for the template,
then select Run now.

51
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:12,199
The page says this renders the export for
checking before an agency sees it, and

52
00:03:12,239 --> 00:03:14,659
audits every included record as an export.

53
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:19,840
The completed run shows a Manual trigger,
two records, three hundred sixteen

54
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:22,620
bytes, a checksum and a Download link.

55
00:03:22,989 --> 00:03:26,690
Download the file and compare its headers
and rows with the intended handoff.

56
00:03:27,239 --> 00:03:31,249
The retained exercise file has the
six selected headers and two training

57
00:03:31,249 --> 00:03:35,360
records, including one amended record
in this finalized-record window.

58
00:03:35,559 --> 00:03:38,559
Return to Edit and
change Schedule to Daily.

59
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:43,460
Set Hour to six in department local
time and keep the thirty-day window.

60
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:47,200
The form also contains weekday
and day-of-month controls for

61
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:51,110
other schedule choices, but this
exercise saves the Daily choice.

62
00:03:51,579 --> 00:03:55,060
Review the hour and window
together, then select Save.

63
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:59,159
Changing a schedule is a configuration
step; the next screen will

64
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:01,179
confirm the stored next-run time.

65
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:04,759
We do not claim that an automatic
run has already occurred.

66
00:04:05,019 --> 00:04:09,039
After saving, Next run shows
November third at six in the morning.

67
00:04:09,409 --> 00:04:13,340
The index independently shows
Daily and the same next-run value.

68
00:04:13,739 --> 00:04:17,439
That is the saved scheduling result
for this dated training exercise.

69
00:04:17,859 --> 00:04:22,250
To leave the department without an
active timer, reopen the template, choose

70
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:24,669
No schedule, and select Save again.

71
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:28,689
Reopening now shows No schedule
with a dash for Next run.

72
00:04:29,130 --> 00:04:32,320
Verify that stored result
instead of assuming an unsaved

73
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,919
selection stopped the schedule.

74
00:04:34,109 --> 00:04:38,170
Use the same configuration and checking
process across department types.

75
00:04:38,540 --> 00:04:42,750
Search-and-rescue teams, security
companies, wildland contractors and

76
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:46,979
industrial emergency teams can standardize
their permitted record handoffs.

77
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:51,139
Community paramedicine and mental
health response teams can define an

78
00:04:51,139 --> 00:04:56,030
appropriate coordination or training
export, as can fire and E M S departments.

79
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:01,120
Start with the right definition and
columns, check a manual file, and verify

80
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,969
the schedule before relying on it.

81
00:05:03,409 --> 00:05:07,589
Delivery through a Workflow is a separate
operation that must be configured and

82
00:05:07,589 --> 00:05:09,640
tested for the intended recipient.


